{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1561632-the-storm-wrought-host-a-sword-sorcery-proximi-dynasty","id":1561632,"title":"The Storm-wrought Host, a sword & sorcery Proximi Dynasty","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-07-12T12:21:18-07:00","id":1561632,"title":"The Storm-wrought Host, a sword & sorcery Proximi Dynasty","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Nickname:</b> Unbowed<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> Since time immemorial, those strong in battle and valorous of heart have been known to hear something beckoning them amid thunderstorms, a summons, a challenge. Those that venture forth and follow the call find themselves struck by lightning, yet no harm comes to them. When the flash of light fades, they find themselves standing before the entrance of an imposing mountain keep standing defiantly against the gathering clouds, a temple of the Ungula Draconis, the Indomitable Citadel.<br /> <br /> Within its halls they shall face a trial, a test of the courage to strive and survive, the strength to vanquish and thrive, the will of steel to overcome all odds. If they fall, they find not death, but wake up at home or amongst friends, with their wounds fully healed, now a Sleepwalker. Should they persevere, upon the final foe falling before them, they give an exultant victory roar and a fierce lightning storm surges forth from them. Windows shatter, the surroundings are overturned, electrical current surges all around them and they are swallowed completely by a brilliant, blinding glare.<br /> <br /> When the light subsides, they realize they are returned from the citadel as an Unbowed, their mana reservoir fully charged, having arrived in a strike of lightning.<br /> <br /> The Citadel Indomitable still holds many secrets even after eons of inquiry, chief amongst them its nature and location, for if either are known, they are not written down in public records. Some have speculated it dwells within an Emanation, others that it is the chantry of a forgotten archmaster and some even theorize it exists somewhere in the Luminous Bastion.<br /> <br /> The Adamantine Arrow claims kinship with the Unbowed, and indeed many join the Order, forging bonds of fellowship with the talons and often finding a common foe in those that abuse the gifts of magic.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> The Unbowed dive into adversity with gusto, seeking to challenge the odds and push beyond their limits. It is common for one to have many scars, for although they might be able to heal them, often they will choose to keep them as a souvenir of their exploits. Warriors one and all, a courageous heart beats in their chest as they carve a path in the world, steadfast in the pursuit of their own code of honor.<br /> <br /> <b>Parent Path:</b> Obrimos<br /> <br /> <b>Blessings of Forces:</b> Environmental Shield, Kinetic Blow, Kinetic Efficiency, Nightvision, Velocity Control.<br /> <b>Blessings of Life:</b> Heightened Senses, Honing the Form, Knit, Mend, Purge Illness<br /> <b>Blessings of Prime: </b>Ephemeral Enchantment, Pierce Deception, Wards &amp; Signs, Words of Truth<br /> <br /> <b>Curse:</b> The call of adventure echoes deeply in the soul of the Unbowed, raging like a mighty storm, urging them to test their strength and wits against life\u2019s challenges, to constantly push against their limits. It drives them to face trials earnestly, and when their inner strength falters, to reignite their passion in the crucible of struggle.<br /> <br /> <b>Persistent:</b> The Unbowed are fiercely competitive, they must give their all in a contest or they will falter. Any time they are in a direct competition with another character, they suffer a -2 die penalty on any rolls where they don\u2019t spend Willpower. This includes contested and extended rolls. In addition, any rolls to tempt or coerce the Unbowed into competition achieve exceptional success on three successes instead of five.<br /> <br /> <b>Beat:</b> Whenever the Unbowed pursues a competition at significant personal risk (social standing, safety, goals, etc) or achieves a decisive victory over a rival, they gain a Beat.<br /> <br /> <b>Oblations:</b> Feasting, revelry, performing feats of endurance, training or sparring, foraging.<br /> <br /> <b>Severe Curse:</b> Whenever the Unbowed incurs a Paradox or runs out of Willpower points, the tempest in their spirit starts to abate and they must endeavor to make the storm roar once more. Should they have any Willpower left, they must roll their points (not dots) as a dice pool, the Unbowed keeps one Willpower point per success and immediately loses the rest. In addition, they cannot regain Willpower from their Virtue, Vice or by supernatural means. In addition they may regain a point by refusing to surrender against challenging odds, defeating a worthy foe in a meaningful competition, winning a pivotal battle, from rest as normal or by other means of regaining Willpower. Whenever they regain all their Willpower back, the Curse recedes to its persistent version.<br /> \u200b</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>What were you thinking design wise ?</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#101010\">Inspired by the world of </span><i><span style=\"color:#101010\">Conan the Barbarian</span></i><span style=\"color:#101010\">, I wanted to create a Proximi lineage with a sword and sorcery feel. Thematically they are meant to feel like they were blessed by Crom with the power to strive and slay, so their spells were chosen to either feel like enhancements of their natural abilities or to help them endure, to give the feel of a badass normal facing the supernatural. Normally blessings are limited to 3 dot effects at the highest, but I chose to include </span><i><span style=\"color:#101010\">Mend </span></i><span style=\"color:#101010\">since it felt thematically appropriate, plus it's not the most powerful spell and has some functionality overlap with </span><i><span style=\"color:#101010\">Knit</span></i><span style=\"color:#101010\">. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\">Although Crom is described as a grim and gloomy god, both he and Conan extoll a philosophy that nothing is impossible, if you have the will to strive towards it. Because of this, I felt he was more aligned with the Aether\u2019s unbound potential rather than the solemn nature of Stygia, with Life as a third Arcana representing the desire to live life as fully as possible.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\">Their persistent curse effectively gives them a permanent version of the Competitive condition, giving them a thematic reason to balance willpower expenditure wisely when competing. By granting them a Beat when they take on these challenges, it gives a mechanical incentive for them to test themselves in all sorts of competitions. The severe version of the curse is based on the Soul Shocked condition, but modified so they do not lose 10-again on the roll and recharge Willpower when they take on worthy challenges. It does allow them to recover Willpower by resting, so they will never be stuck with a frustrating struggle with the curse, but by taking on a more difficult path, their Willpower recovers faster. The more Willpower points they have left, the more likely it is for them to quickly shake off the severe curse, but they can risk making it worse . Which means the most valuable an Unbowed has to manage is their Willpower, which feels in line with the answer of the Riddle of Steel (</span><i><span style=\"color:#101010\">\u201cIron breaks, flesh falters, but a will of steel forged in the crucible of struggle conquers all\u201d</span></i><span style=\"color:#101010\">). The oblations encourage them to live deeply and are inspired by some of the actions Conan did in his downtime.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\">Their appearance portrays them as enjoying every minute of facing an ordeal, having a warrior\u2019s spirit and closely following their own code, similar to Conan.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\">Since Crom does not bestow any blessings save will and the strength to endure, it seemed fitting that this type of Proximi must earn their abilities through a trial. Crom is said to dwell atop the greatest of mountains, so fittingly the test happens in his fortress. In addition, his symbol is a mountain struck by lightning, and he is seen as a storm deity, so both figure prominently in the aesthetic. Storms symbolize intense trials, conflict and chaos. Lightning symbolizes intuition, illumination and destruction. The warriors who undertake the challenge reforge their mettle in the power of the storm, and even those that fail have shown sufficient bravery to warrant being Sleepwalkers, and perhaps a future attempt. The lightning storm at the completion of the trial is inspired by the Quickening from </span><i><span style=\"color:#101010\">Highlander</span></i><span style=\"color:#101010\">.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\">The fact they have an inclination to fight those that abuse magic was a suggestion by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27436_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27436\" data-vbnamecard=\"27436\">CalvinSiler</a>, who pointed out Conan had a tendency to fight corrupt mages. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#101010\">The history of Crom is left deliberately vague. Was he slain and the Citadel is his wending ? Did he Ascend as some kind of symbol of the indomitable human spirit ? Does he still travel the world ? The answer is left open as a potential plot hook.</span><br /> <br /> That concludes the design notes, hope you had as much fun reading them as I had writing them. A big thanks to NuriaAge and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27436_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27436\" data-vbnamecard=\"27436\">CalvinSiler</a> for their feedback.<br /> \u200b</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-13T11:02:35-07:00","id":1561655,"title":"","content":"Can these people pass their power on to children?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-13T11:46:38-07:00","id":1561656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1561632-the-storm-wrought-host-a-sword-sorcery-proximi-dynasty?p=1561655#post1561655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can these people pass their power on to children?</div> </div> </div> </div>I leave that deliberately open, should you prefer for all Proximi to have to earn their abilities, but I think it could work just as fine if they can pass it on, whichever seems more fun for your chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=